Z||000004||Kevin-84SE||01-30-2001||09:00 PM||||A few months ago, I took my 84 SE up to the local dealer to have the e-brake recall done on it, I know it was never done because I have had the car since new and the last time the car was at a dealer was in 1989 and the recall was issued in 1991 (I have all records for the car) also I have the recall notice and card that needs to be sent in when the recall is completed. The dealer said the  VISS database indicates that there are no  open recalls for my car. He could not tell me when the recall was performed, he said that if the database does not have a recall listed then he can't do it. A month or so later I was searching this forum and found out that I could tell if the recall had been done or not by looking at the caliper pistons, I checked the calipers and found that I do have the yellow check valves in the center and not solid pistons indicating that the recall had not been done. I called Pontiac December 14 2000 and they said their Database did not go back that far and that if the VISS database that the dealer uses does not indicate any recalls for my VIN then they can't do anything about it. <BR>After about 3 hours on the phone with them I found out that the dealers VISS database does not go back to 1984 so they don't have any record of my car which is why they can't tell me when the recall was done I think they said it only goes back to 1989. Basically I told them that I could prove it was not done and since they could not prove that it was done  I demanded that they perform the recall. I told them that I would call The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration. Pontiac had a discussion with the dealer and the dealer agreed to perform the recall. I have not had my car back together since so I have not had a chance to take it in for the recall yet. I will probably be April or May before I can take it in, I hope they will do the recall then. <P>I think that if what they told me is true that the VISS system only goes back to 1989 then any Fiero VIN they put in will come up with no open recalls even if they have never been done. Has anyone had any success getting a recall done on a Fiero recently? if so what year Fiero and when?<P>   Kevin||||reg||1
